id: pm-xa1w84
title: Guard telemetry metrics storage and readiness against unsupported filesystems
description: "The metrics service crashed after its TSDB volume resolved onto an unsupported filesystem. Recovery preserved all data and restored local POSIX storage, but deployment and storage relocation currently lack a preventive filesystem/readiness check."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: changelog-exclude,observability,operations,telemetry
created_at: "2026-10-12T22:55:55.643Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-12T05:20:59.409Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Validate actual filesystem backing before starting Prometheus; fail visibly for unsupported storage; preserve rollback; monitor readiness and scrape freshness; prove a negative control without production data.
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: medium
confidence: high
expected_result: "A deployment preflight rejects unsupported TSDB storage, readiness and scrape freshness are measured, and a controlled unsupported-storage case proves the guard."
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-m1tfmp,discovered_from,"2026-10-12T22:55:55.643Z","harness:codex","cli:create:dep",detected
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-12T22:55:55.643Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete all-status corpus and current request-specific storage/readiness search contain recovery incident pm-m1tfmp and completed dashboard/pipeline work but no preventive TSDB filesystem guard. This follow-up remains open and unclaimed; it does not reopen completed telemetry implementation."
  "2026-11-12T05:20:59.408Z","harness:claude-code","Progress 2026-11-12 (pm-xcndcu renewed the pm-m1tfmp waiver on this evidence). The private telemetry stack health check now has a read-only Prometheus section: it fails visibly when the TSDB mount is not local POSIX storage (ext4, xfs or btrfs), when Prometheus is not ready, or when any active scrape target is down or more than five minutes stale. Today it reports tsdb_fs ext4, ready, zero restarts, six of six targets up and fresh. Still open for this item: a deployment-time preflight that refuses to start Prometheus on unsupported storage, and a negative control without production data. Changing the production compose stack needs the maintainer, so it was not done in this pass.\n"
body: ""
